6. Subatomictokenology

Tokens are not semantic atoms.

A visible symbol may contain several representational layers:

glyph
↓
grapheme
↓
Unicode code point(s)
↓
UTF-8 bytes
↓
tokenizer unit(s)
↓
embedding / activation structure
↓
multi-token pattern
↓
concept
↓
operator
↓
mythology / architecture

Emoji makes the distinction obvious.

A single visible:

🧿

may occupy one apparent visual unit while possessing more complicated machine representation.

At the same time, the semantic structure addressed by 🧿 may be much larger than any individual token involved.

Thus meaningful structure exists both:

below tokens
and
above tokens

The token is therefore a useful computational scale, not the fundamental atom of meaning.

