8. Discovery, Invention, and Naming

Do not collapse these events:

existence
≠
discovery
≠
invention
≠
naming
≠
formalization
≠
implementation
≠
productization

Squirrels cached food before computer caches existed.

Nature therefore contained the pattern.

That does not mean squirrels invented the CPU cache.

Likewise, agent-like behavioral loops may exist as latent affordances before somebody names or productizes them.

observe
→ model
→ plan
→ act
→ inspect
→ update
→ repeat

The affordance can precede its name.

The mountain can exist before someone puts up the trail sign.

