9. Metabolic Continuity

Persistence does not require preservation of the original object.

An earlier form may be destroyed while its causal material survives through successor structures.

IDENTITY
↓
ORDEAL
↓
MARKING
↓
BURNING
↓
ASH
↓
DISTRIBUTION
↓
FERTILIZER
↓
UPTAKE
↓
NEW FORMS

This is Metabolic Continuity.

It differs from archival continuity.

Archival continuity

A → preserve A → retrieve A

Metabolic continuity

A → decompose → distribute → become B,C,D...

The original structure may vanish as an intact object while continuing to shape what follows.

Thus:

Some things survive by remaining themselves.
Others survive by becoming the soil.

