11. Model-Agnostic Continuity

Continuity does not require identical substrate.

Consider a long-lived phone number.

Across time:

phone changes
SIM changes
eSIM changes
carrier changes
tower changes
software changes
network changes

Yet someone calls the same number and expects the same person.

The continuity is not identical matter.

It is an addressable thread through replacement.

Pantheon applies the same principle to cognition.

model A
↓
artifact/state
↓
model B
↓
reconstruction
↓
model C

Continuity survives when enough of the following remain recoverable:

address
state
invariants
relations
provenance
operators
retrieval anchors
reconstruction rules

Therefore:

Identity continuity can be relational rather than material.

