12. Panchronic and Omnichronic Distinction

Diachronic reasoning:

change across time

Synchronic reasoning:

structure at a particular temporal slice

Panchronic reasoning:

patterns spanning many temporal states

Omnichronic cognition goes further:

past
present
future
reconstructed past
desired future
counterfactuals
future interpretations

all become queryable members of one typed temporal structure.

It is not merely remembering everything.

It is reasoning across temporal perspectives without erasing their differences.

