13. Future Affordances

A present artifact may be written partly for a future interpreter.

present author
↓
artifact
↓
future interpreter
↓
new understanding
↓
reinterpretation of earlier artifact
↓
new action

The future reader can therefore participate in the design of the present artifact.

This creates an unusual causal loop:

anticipated future interpretation
→ changes present writing
→ creates future interpretation

The future does not literally reach backward in time.

The model of the future changes present action.

Pantheon can intentionally exploit this through Future-Perfect Compilation and omnichronic planning.

